{
 "esm": "1.3.0",
 "metadata": {
  "name": "mosart_hillslope",
  "description": "MOSART hillslope routing step (stage 2 of the EqESM project): the per-cell Euler step 1 of mosart_physics.F90:Euler (F90:74-80) composed of hillslopeRouting (F90:225-239) and updateState_hillslope (F90:352-360), written as a storage ODE with the pointwise laws imported from ./mosart_templates.esm. Equations, exactly as in the Fortran: ehout_manning = -CREHT_nosqrt(hslpsqrt, nh, Gxr, yh) (F90:232); the dry-cell clamp replaces ehout by -(qsur + wh/delt) when ehout < 0 and wh + (qsur + ehout)*delt < TINYVALUE (F90:233-236); dwh = qsur + ehout (F90:237); d(wh)/dt = dwh (the Euler storage advance wh += dwh*DeltaT, F90:77, in continuous limit); yh = wh (updateState_hillslope, F90:358); and the lateral inflow to the subnetwork etin = (-ehout + qsub)*area*frac (F90:79). Units per mosart_tstatusflux_type.F90 / mosart_tspatialunit_type.F90: wh, yh [m]; dwh, qsur, qsub, ehout [m/s]; etin [m3/s]; hslpsqrt [1]; Gxr [1/m]; area [m2]; frac [1]; nh is the hillslope Manning roughness (SI dimension s/m^(1/3), see mosart_templates.esm); delt is Tctl%DeltaT = delt_coupling/nsub (mosart_driver.F90:800). The qsur/qsub forcing arrives from the cap in m/s (mosart_driver.F90:806-813 converts the m3/s streams by /area). The tests block pins the overland law CREHT_nosqrt pointwise (instantaneous D-boundary tests, time_span {0,0}) and the one-substep storage traces in the continuous-ODE form, with numeric tuples from the stage-1 instrumentation dumps (stage1/dumps/mosart/creht_nosqrt.csv, mosart_euler.csv); the trace assertions carry the measured Euler-vs-continuous scheme gaps (see README.md (Testing)). Reference: stage1/cesm/components/mosart/src/riverroute/mosart_physics.F90 (mosart1.1.13).",
   "tags": [
    "environmental_transport",
    "mosart",
    "river-routing",
    "hydrology",
    "hillslope",
    "overland-flow",
    "manning",
    "cesm"
   ],
   "created": "2026-10-26T00:00:00Z",
   "authors": [
    "EqESM project contributors"
   ],
   "references": [
    {
     "citation": "Li, H., Wigmosta, M. S., Wu, H., Huang, M., Ke, Y., Coleman, A. M., and Leung, L. R. (2013). A physically based runoff routing model for land surface and earth system models. Journal of Hydrometeorology, 14(3), 808-828. The MOSART (Model for Scale Adaptive River Transport) routing scheme these components transcribe.",
     "doi": "10.1175/JHM-D-12-015.1"
    },
    {
     "citation": "CESM (Community Earth System Model), ESCOMP/CESM, cesm3.0-alphabranch: MOSART river-routing source (mosart1.1.13) - mosart_physics.F90, mosart_driver.F90, mosart_tstatusflux_type.F90, mosart_tspatialunit_type.F90, rof_comp_nuopc/rof_import_export.F90 - the reference implementation these components are transcribed from.",
     "url": "https://github.com/ESCOMP/CESM"
    },
    {
     "citation": "EarthSciModels - the authoritative .esm corpus this component lives in.",
     "url": "https://github.com/EarthSciML/EarthSciModels"
    }
   ]
 },
 "models": {
  "Hillslope": {
   "expression_template_imports": [
    { "ref": "./mosart_templates.esm" }
   ],
   "variables": {
    "wh": {
     "type": "unknown",
     "units": "m",
     "default": 0.0,
     "description": "storage of surface water at the hillslope (TRunoff%wh), [m]"
    },
    "dwh": {
     "type": "unknown",
     "units": "m/s",
     "description": "change of hillslope water storage (TRunoff%dwh) = qsur + ehout, [m/s]"
    },
    "yh": {
     "type": "unknown",
     "units": "m",
     "description": "depth of surface water (TRunoff%yh), defined by updateState_hillslope as yh = wh, [m]"
    },
    "ehout_manning": {
     "type": "unknown",
     "units": "m/s",
     "description": "unclamped overland flow from the hillslope into the sub-network channels, -CREHT_nosqrt(...), [m/s]"
    },
    "ehout": {
     "type": "unknown",
     "units": "m/s",
     "description": "overland flow after the dry-cell clamp of hillslopeRouting (TRunoff%ehout), [m/s]"
    },
    "etin": {
     "type": "unknown",
     "units": "m^3/s",
     "description": "lateral inflow from hillslope into the subnetwork (TRunoff%etin) = (-ehout + qsub)*area*frac, [m3/s]"
    },
    "qsur": {
     "type": "parameter",
     "units": "m/s",
     "default": 0.0,
     "description": "surface runoff generated from the hillslope (TRunoff%qsur, after the mosart_driver m3/s -> m/s /area conversion), [m/s]"
    },
    "qsub": {
     "type": "parameter",
     "units": "m/s",
     "default": 0.0,
     "description": "subsurface runoff generated from the hillslope (TRunoff%qsub), [m/s]"
    },
    "hslpsqrt": {
     "type": "parameter",
     "units": "1",
     "default": 0.01,
     "description": "sqrt of the hillslope slope (TUnit%hslpsqrt, from the frivinp network file hslp), [-]"
    },
    "nh": {
     "type": "parameter",
     "units": "s/m^(1/3)",
     "default": 0.03,
     "description": "Manning's roughness of the hillslope, channel network excluded (TUnit%nh, from frivinp); network file stores a bare number; declared with its SI dimension s/m^(1/3) for dimensional consistency"
    },
    "Gxr": {
     "type": "parameter",
     "units": "1/m",
     "default": 0.001,
     "description": "drainage density within the cell (TUnit%Gxr, from frivinp gxr), [1/m]"
    },
    "area": {
     "type": "parameter",
     "units": "m^2",
     "default": 10000000.0,
     "description": "area of the local cell (TUnit%area, from frivinp), [m2]"
    },
    "frac": {
     "type": "parameter",
     "units": "1",
     "default": 1.0,
     "description": "fraction of the cell included in the study area (TUnit%frac, from frivinp), [-]"
    },
    "delt": {
     "type": "parameter",
     "units": "s",
     "default": 3600.0,
     "description": "routing substep Tctl%DeltaT = delt_coupling/nsub (mosart_driver.F90:800), [s]"
    }
   },
   "equations": [
    {
     "lhs": "ehout_manning",
     "rhs": {
      "op": "*",
      "args": [
       -1.0,
       { "op": "apply_expression_template", "args": [], "name": "overland_discharge",
         "bindings": { "sqrthslp": "hslpsqrt", "nh": "nh", "Gxr": "Gxr", "yh": "yh" } }
      ]
     }
    },
    {
     "lhs": "ehout",
     "rhs": {
      "op": "ifelse",
      "args": [
       { "op": "and", "args": [
         { "op": "<", "args": ["ehout_manning", 0.0] },
         { "op": "<", "args": [
           { "op": "+", "args": [
             "wh",
             { "op": "*", "args": [
               { "op": "+", "args": ["qsur", "ehout_manning"] },
               "delt" ] } ] },
           1.0e-14 ] } ] },
       { "op": "*", "args": [
         -1.0,
         { "op": "+", "args": ["qsur", { "op": "/", "args": ["wh", "delt"] }] } ] },
       "ehout_manning"
      ]
     }
    },
    {
     "lhs": "dwh",
     "rhs": { "op": "+", "args": ["qsur", "ehout"] }
    },
    {
     "lhs": { "op": "D", "args": ["wh"], "wrt": "t" },
     "rhs": "dwh"
    },
    {
     "lhs": "yh",
     "rhs": "wh"
    },
    {
     "lhs": "etin",
     "rhs": {
      "op": "*",
      "args": [
       { "op": "+", "args": [{ "op": "-", "args": ["ehout"] }, "qsub"] },
       "area",
       "frac"
      ]
     }
    }
   ],
   "tests": [
    {
     "id": "overland_law_step1_sub2_cell100312",
     "description": "Instantaneous pin of the overland-flow law CREHT_nosqrt at the hillslope (mosart_physics.F90:426-437) from stage1/dumps/mosart/creht_nosqrt.csv row (step 1, ns 2, nr 1, gindex 100312): yh = wh = 9.32660989523826711e-11 m, sqrthslp = 3.78813938497516212e-01, nh = 7.74544477462768555e-02, Gxr = 2.99999999999999974e-04 give ehout_manning = -CREHT_nosqrt = eht_raw = -2.81432250323167531e-20 m/s, and etin = (-ehout + qsub)*area*frac = 8.16213652457282613e-11 m3/s with area = 2.900213644740529e9 m2 (the qsur_m3s/qsur_ms ratio of the step-1 dump rows; qsur = 2.59072497089951852e-14 m/s from mosart_euler.csv row (1,2,entry,100312)). time_span {0,0} keeps wh at its initial condition so the law is evaluated pointwise; the dry-cell clamp does not fire (wh + (qsur + ehout)*delt = 1.87e-10 > TINYVALUE). The Fortran value is reproduced to round-off (rel 1e-12; cross-language pow() ulps).",
     "time_span": { "start": 0.0, "end": 0.0 },
     "parameter_overrides": {
      "qsur": 2.59072497089951852e-14,
      "qsub": 0.0,
      "hslpsqrt": 3.78813938497516212e-01,
      "nh": 7.74544477462768555e-02,
      "Gxr": 2.99999999999999974e-04,
      "area": 2900213644.740529,
      "frac": 1.0,
      "delt": 3600.0
     },
     "initial_conditions": { "wh": 9.32660989523826711e-11 },
     "tolerance": { "rel": 1e-12, "abs": 1e-26 },
     "assertions": [
      { "variable": "yh", "time": 0.0, "expected": 9.32660989523826711e-11 },
      { "variable": "ehout_manning", "time": 0.0, "expected": -2.81432250323167531e-20 },
      { "variable": "ehout", "time": 0.0, "expected": -2.81432250323167531e-20 },
      { "variable": "etin", "time": 0.0, "expected": 8.16213652457282613e-11 }
     ]
    },
    {
     "id": "overland_law_drain_cell101032",
     "description": "Instantaneous pin of CREHT_nosqrt from creht_nosqrt.csv row (step 5, ns 1, nr 4, gindex 101032), a cell with a steeper hillslope: yh = 2.79791921922257878e-10 m, sqrthslp = 3.88458491991100663e-01, nh = 7.58072286844253540e-02, Gxr = 2.99999999999999974e-04 give eht_raw = ehout = -1.83998326708271600e-19 m/s (qsur = qsub = 0 in step 5, mosart_euler.csv row (5,1,entry,101032); the clamp cannot fire with qsur = 0 and wh > TINYVALUE).",
     "time_span": { "start": 0.0, "end": 0.0 },
     "parameter_overrides": {
      "qsur": 0.0,
      "qsub": 0.0,
      "hslpsqrt": 3.88458491991100663e-01,
      "nh": 7.58072286844253540e-02,
      "Gxr": 2.99999999999999974e-04,
      "delt": 3600.0
     },
     "initial_conditions": { "wh": 2.79791921922257878e-10 },
     "tolerance": { "rel": 1e-12, "abs": 1e-26 },
     "assertions": [
      { "variable": "yh", "time": 0.0, "expected": 2.79791921922257878e-10 },
      { "variable": "ehout_manning", "time": 0.0, "expected": -1.83998326708271600e-19 },
      { "variable": "ehout", "time": 0.0, "expected": -1.83998326708271600e-19 }
     ]
    },
    {
     "id": "overland_law_drain_cell100313",
     "description": "Instantaneous pin of CREHT_nosqrt from creht_nosqrt.csv row (step 5, ns 1, nr 2, gindex 100313): yh = 1.39897800399400462e-10 m, sqrthslp = 2.68886593194975043e-01, nh = 7.85291716456413269e-02, Gxr = 2.99999999999999974e-04 give eht_raw = ehout = -3.87267332350159691e-20 m/s. Varied mid-range inputs relative to the other law tests.",
     "time_span": { "start": 0.0, "end": 0.0 },
     "parameter_overrides": {
      "qsur": 0.0,
      "qsub": 0.0,
      "hslpsqrt": 2.68886593194975043e-01,
      "nh": 7.85291716456413269e-02,
      "Gxr": 2.99999999999999974e-04,
      "delt": 3600.0
     },
     "initial_conditions": { "wh": 1.39897800399400462e-10 },
     "tolerance": { "rel": 1e-12, "abs": 1e-26 },
     "assertions": [
      { "variable": "yh", "time": 0.0, "expected": 1.39897800399400462e-10 },
      { "variable": "ehout_manning", "time": 0.0, "expected": -3.87267332350159691e-20 },
      { "variable": "ehout", "time": 0.0, "expected": -3.87267332350159691e-20 }
     ]
    },
    {
     "id": "overland_law_zero_storage",
     "description": "Zero-storage pin from creht_nosqrt.csv row (step 1, ns 1, nr 1, gindex 100312): with yh = wh = 0 the Manning velocity is zeroed by the rr <= 0 guard and CREHT_nosqrt returns 0, so ehout_manning = ehout = -0 (eht_raw = -0 in the dump) and etin = 0 even with qsur = 2.59072497089951852e-14 m/s.",
     "time_span": { "start": 0.0, "end": 0.0 },
     "parameter_overrides": {
      "qsur": 2.59072497089951852e-14,
      "qsub": 0.0,
      "hslpsqrt": 3.78813938497516212e-01,
      "nh": 7.74544477462768555e-02,
      "Gxr": 2.99999999999999974e-04,
      "area": 2900213644.740529,
      "frac": 1.0,
      "delt": 3600.0
     },
     "initial_conditions": { "wh": 0.0 },
     "tolerance": { "rel": 1e-12, "abs": 1e-26 },
     "assertions": [
      { "variable": "yh", "time": 0.0, "expected": 0.0 },
      { "variable": "ehout_manning", "time": 0.0, "expected": 0.0 },
      { "variable": "ehout", "time": 0.0, "expected": 0.0 },
      { "variable": "etin", "time": 0.0, "expected": 0.0 }
     ]
    },
    {
     "id": "one_step_growth_step1_sub2",
     "description": "One-substep trace in the continuous-ODE form over [0, 3600] (delt = Tctl%DeltaT from the mosart_euler.csv delt column): entry (step 1, ns 2, gindex 100312) wh = 9.32660989523826711e-11 m with qsur = 2.59072497089951852e-14 m/s, qsub = 0; the exit state (step 1, ns 2) is wh = 1.86532096589155226e-10 m, ehout = -2.81432250323167531e-20 m/s, etin = 8.16213652457282613e-11 m3/s (area = 2.900213644740529e9 m2, the qsur_m3s/qsur_ms ratio of the step-1 dump rows). The .esm integrates d(wh)/dt = qsur + ehout(wh) continuously while the Fortran advances wh += dwh*DeltaT with the law held at the substep-start depth (Euler step 1, F90:77); the measured scheme gap (continuous-ODE end state vs the Fortran's single Euler step, solver at reltol 1e-14) is 1.02e-17 m abs on wh = 5.5e-8 rel of the end state - the rel 1e-5 assertion bound is ~2x the measured gap.",
     "time_span": { "start": 0.0, "end": 3600.0 },
     "parameter_overrides": {
      "qsur": 2.59072497089951852e-14,
      "qsub": 0.0,
      "hslpsqrt": 3.78813938497516212e-01,
      "nh": 7.74544477462768555e-02,
      "Gxr": 2.99999999999999974e-04,
      "area": 2900213644.740529,
      "frac": 1.0,
      "delt": 3600.0
     },
     "initial_conditions": { "wh": 9.32660989523826711e-11 },
     "tolerance": { "rel": 1e-5, "abs": 1e-16 },
     "assertions": [
      { "variable": "wh", "time": 3600.0, "expected": 1.86532096589155226e-10 },
      { "variable": "ehout", "time": 0.0, "expected": -2.81432250323167531e-20 },
      { "variable": "etin", "time": 0.0, "expected": 8.16213652457282613e-11 }
     ]
    },
    {
     "id": "one_step_drain_step2_sub1",
     "description": "One-substep drain trace over [0, 3600]: entry (step 2, ns 1, gindex 100312) wh = 2.79797873884816915e-10 m with qsur = qsub = 0 (step-2 imports carry no runoff); the exit state (step 2, ns 1) is wh = 2.79797241651524941e-10 m. The ehout/etin assertions sit at time 0, where the state is the entry state and the law values equal the Fortran's substep values (ehout = -1.75620358877005223e-19 m/s, etin = 5.09336561109318995e-10 m3/s at the entry depth). With qsur = 0 the storage drains through the overland law only; the measured scheme gap (continuous-ODE end state vs the Fortran's single Euler step, solver at reltol 1e-14) is 1.19e-21 m abs on wh = 4.3e-12 rel of the end state (the Euler second-order term of the tiny relative drain of 2.3e-6 per step) - the rel 1e-7 bound is >1000x the measured gap.",
     "time_span": { "start": 0.0, "end": 3600.0 },
     "parameter_overrides": {
      "qsur": 0.0,
      "qsub": 0.0,
      "hslpsqrt": 3.78813938497516212e-01,
      "nh": 7.74544477462768555e-02,
      "Gxr": 2.99999999999999974e-04,
      "area": 2900213644.740529,
      "frac": 1.0,
      "delt": 3600.0
     },
     "initial_conditions": { "wh": 2.79797873884816915e-10 },
     "tolerance": { "rel": 1e-7, "abs": 1e-17 },
     "assertions": [
      { "variable": "wh", "time": 3600.0, "expected": 2.79797241651524941e-10 },
      { "variable": "ehout", "time": 0.0, "expected": -1.75620358877005223e-19 },
      { "variable": "etin", "time": 0.0, "expected": 5.09336561109318995e-10 }
     ]
    }
   ]
  }
 }
}
